+# Browser speech integration
+Piper speech connected to all six mascot Speak controls and the response reader. Explicit ES/EN selector; default 100% volume; cancellation ignores late downloads. Speech stays on the visitor device; only public model files are downloaded. No inference billing.
+
+Dependencies: @mintplex-labs/piper-tts-web 1.0.5 (MIT), locally vendored; changed singleton reuse to require identical voice, one ONNX thread, pinned ONNX runtime 1.18.0 (MIT), rhasspy model URLs. Piper phonemizer uses espeak-ng (GPLv3); source and build: https://github.com/diffusion-studio/piper-wasm and https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng . WASM files served by pinned upstream package @diffusionstudio/piper-wasm@1.0.0. ONNX WASM pinned 1.18.0.
+
+Spanish: es_MX-ald-medium; model card specifies Unlicense dataset. English: en_US-ljspeech-medium; model card specifies public-domain dataset, trained from scratch. Model cards: https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices/blob/main/es/es_MX/ald/medium/MODEL_CARD and https://huggingface.co/rhasspy/piper-voices/blob/main/en/en_US/ljspeech/medium/MODEL_CARD .
+
+This does not embed or redistribute the Maney demonstration voice (license unverified). The previous approved Maney sample is a separate external demonstration. No singing synthesis added. First use downloads about 65 MB per voice, plus runtime. Requires an open compatible browser; does not enable background audio with laptop closed.
